  "derivation": "Synthetic fixture. State: patterns DEAD, LIVE, WIND; combination COMB1 (linear_add) with items (DEAD, load_pattern) 1, (LIVE, load_pattern) 1, (ENV1, load_combination, step Max) 1, (ENV1, load_combination, step Min) 1; combination ENV1 (envelope) with (DEAD, load_pattern) 1. e1 replaces COMB1 as type envelope with terms (DEAD, load_pattern) 2, (WIND, load_pattern) 0.5, (ENV1, load_combination, Max) 1. The combination is in the state: a `set` of /type on [combinations, COMB1] (value envelope). Each term is matched to the state's items by the D2 item key (case, case_type, step; a null step is left out): DEAD/load_pattern is held, so a `set` of /scale_ratio 2 on [combinations, COMB1, items, DEAD, load_pattern]; WIND/load_pattern is not held, so an `add` of the whole item {case {case WIND, case_type load_pattern, step null}, scale_ratio 0.5}; ENV1/load_combination/Max is held with scale 1, so a `set` of /scale_ratio 1 (a no-op write). The held keys the set leaves out, LIVE/load_pattern and ENV1/load_combination/Min, are `remove`. The pattern DEAD and the combination ENV1 are not confused with any other key because case_type and step are part of the key. Sorted by key member by member (a key before every longer key it begins; DEAD < ENV1 < LIVE < WIND; Max < Min): type, DEAD, ENV1 Max, ENV1 Min, LIVE, WIND: ids e1/1 to e1/6. e2 defines the new combination COMB2 (linear_add) of (DEAD, load_pattern) 1 and (LIVE, load_pattern) 0.5: the state lacks it, so one `add` of the whole object, items in the change set's order (spec 0007 Q15, open); its key sorts after every COMB1 key, and it keeps the id e2.",
